{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'served ledger|items.*sqlite' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{claude-r74*,codex-r74*.md,round74*-brief.md} | cut -c1-450 | head -55\nrg -n 'original_day|source_uri|create table.*evidence' src/hivemind | rg -i 'not null|text|insert into' | head -70\"","aggregated_output":"docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74d.md:19:2. **Clean up on a database failure before publication.** Revision 4 claims `--out` before reading the items database, but specifies cleanup only for `ReleaseRefused` and `OSError`. I verified in memory that querying a database without an `items` table raises `sqlite3.OperationalError`, outside both named cases. As written, that leaves an empty `--out` after an ordinary command failure, and\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.md:11:| **5. Diagnostic columns** | **Closed.** The two optional judgement columns are read only where present, and the report records their absence. I verified that the served ledger has `reasons` and `why_changed` and lacks both `implied_outcome` and `reference`. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:339](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:339) |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:16:**Claude is right about what the production extraction request sees.** For an existing question, it sends the ID, object, due day, question and a description of what evidence belongs there. It sends no stored rung, rung label or judged position. The response schema asks the model to *write* labels for newly proposed questions. `research_context.Reader` really does load stored rungs and the \ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:28:5. **Make the four-store acceptance runnable.** Step 7 asks for `judgements.implied_outcome` and `reference` on every store. I checked the served ledger’s actual schema. It has neither column. Read the available diagnostic columns and report the two as absent on that ledger. Otherwise the specified acceptance can fail on a valid package before it finishes. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:261](/Users/lchi\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md:23:     served ledger's \"Restriction adopted\" labels, and a legacy store with no key table;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md:43:  and 25.4% of the evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and on 35.0% in the served ledger\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:5:I checked the three comparison stores and the served ledger read-only. I found **no confirmed case of a stored judgement being copied into an evidence record**. I did find a meaningful difference between the article, the system’s summary of it, and the system’s own answer. The build design treats all three as strings.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:33:- **Tests 3, 4, 5, 6 and 11** need fixtures that distinguish the branches. Defaulting to `number` passes test 3 even if the unresolved report lists every number question. Assert a condition-only *resolved* question is absent from that report and an unresolved one is present, both with and without a key. For test 6 use the served ledger’s `v49` labels, **“Restriction adopted” / “No restrictio\nsrc/hivemind/extraction.py:568:    \"\"\"D203: original_day is the day the statement was made, as an ISO day, or '' when the text does not state a day. A month, a\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:19:    'evidence': 'evidence_id text primary key, quote text, one_line text, speaker text, original_who text, original_day text, tier text, event_time text, created_seq integer, created_from_input text',\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
