{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/live_lock.py | sed -n '109,145p'\"","aggregated_output":"   109\tdef snapshot(store_path, destination):\n   110\t    \"\"\"A consistent copy of a store, even while it is written: only to a new path (so never onto the store itself); made in a temporary\n   111\t    file beside the destination, taken out of WAL mode, integrity checked, then published by a hard link that fails if the destination\n   112\t    has appeared meanwhile. On any failure nothing created by this call is left. Returns the destination.\"\"\"\n   113\t    real, _ = own_path(store_path)\n   114\t    destination = os.path.abspath(destination)\n   115\t    if os.path.lexists(destination):\n   116\t        raise FileExistsError(f'{destination} exists: a snapshot is written only to a new path')\n   117\t    descriptor, temporary = tempfile.mkstemp(prefix='.snapshot-', suffix='.sqlite', dir=os.path.dirname(destination) or '.')\n   118\t    os.close(descriptor)\n   119\t    source = target = None\n   120\t    try:\n   121\t        try:\n   122\t            source = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{real}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   123\t            target = sqlite3.connect(temporary)\n   124\t            source.backup(target)\n   125\t            leave_wal_mode(target)\n   126\t            check = target.execute('pragma integrity_check').fetchone()[0]\n   127\t            if check != 'ok':\n   128\t                raise RuntimeError(f'the snapshot failed its integrity check: {check}')\n   129\t        finally:\n   130\t            for connection in (target, source):\n   131\t                if connection is not None:\n   132\t                    connection.close()\n   133\t        os.link(temporary, destination)                      # fails if the destination appeared during the copy: nothing is replaced\n   134\t        return destination\n   135\t    finally:\n   136\t        for leftover in (temporary, temporary + '-journal', temporary + '-wal', temporary + '-shm'):\n   137\t            if os.path.exists(leftover):\n   138\t                os.remove(leftover)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"agent_message","text":"**Not ready to build.** Both 74g overwrite findings are closed. Two issues remain in how the command reports success and how the tests verify it.\n\n1. **Both overwrite cases are closed.** `check` now creates the report with `os.link`. If a case-variant name already identifies the items database, the link fails and the database survives. `build` uses the same operation, so a file created at the report name while the build runs also survives. Tests 18 and 19 cover the database hash and the late-arriving marker respectively. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:56](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:56) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:363](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:363)\n\n2. **The builder can tell the operator a report is missing after it has published it.** Step 8 creates the public link, then removes the temporary name. If that removal fails, the complete report already exists, but the specified error says “report not written” and directs the operator to retry. A retry encounters the existing report and exits 2 again. Treat a successful link as the point when the report is published. A later cleanup error should identify the leftover temporary file. The decisive test forces only that removal to fail and verifies that the command correctly identifies the published report. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:192](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:192) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:200](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:200)\n\n3. **The end-to-end tests need an explicit expected exit status.** Test 11 says a successful build then “passes `check`,” but the build has already created the report, so the specified `check` command exits 2. Test 19 has the same issue while its marker occupies the report name. With the occupant in place, assert that `check` prints the successful package result, exits 2, and preserves the occupant. For the exit-0 case, remove the test-owned report first and verify that `check` creates a fresh one. This lets an engineer distinguish a valid package from a failed package check. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:204](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:204) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:342](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:342) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:366](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:366)\n\nI found no other serious blocker in slice 1."}}
